    name="4 Estimation, Analysis, and Statistical Modeling Value Stream"
    id="id-321b6e055742429399b9035b2a8f1fc7"
    documentation="Purpose:&#xD;&#xA;To transform prepared data into analytical insights, estimates, and statistical measures that represent real-world phenomena accurately and impartially.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Description:&#xD;&#xA;This value stream includes all activities related to statistical estimation, weighting, calibration, and model-based inference. It represents the point where methodological expertise adds significant value, converting data into knowledge. Closed-loop validation ensures that outputs meet statistical quality standards and methodological integrity.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;The resulting artefact — an estimated or analyzed dataset — embodies representativeness and statistical soundness, forming the analytical foundation for composed products and indicators.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Key capabilities: Estimation &amp; Weighting, Statistical Modelling, Analytical Design, Methodology Management, Quality Framework Governance."
    viewpoint="value_stream">
